# Spell Queller's enters ability targets a spell of its controller's own as well as an opponent's, and none of mana value 5:
# Bot2 casts Traumatic Critique with X 3 at Bot1 (mana value 5, the X counted, CR 202.3e and the ruling); Bot1 responds
# with two Bolts at Bot2, then flashes in Spell Queller, whose ability cannot target the Critique (the refusal) and exiles
# one of Bot1's own Bolts (CR 115.1: its "target spell" has no "an opponent controls"). The Critique deals Bot1 3 and the
# other Bolt Bot2 3. The Queller has flying. On turn 3 Bot1 sacrifices it to Ashnod's Altar: the exiled card's owner is
# Bot1 itself, who casts the Bolt free (CR 608.2g, 118.9) at Bot2 - the Altar's {C}{C} still floating.

